    h('Online versus offline')
    p('Offline jobs fit preprocessing, train chemical and risk models, select thresholds, validate candidates and publish a versioned checkpoint. Laboratory measurement is external and may take much longer than inference. Online screening starts only when the purchase and compatible laboratory record are available. Validate the declared class, feature order, source-scale compatibility, finiteness and linkage before scoring. Chemical inference may be precomputed per sample.')
    h('Hybrid serving and workload')
    p('A laboratory workstation or small CPU service computes chemical probabilities near the measurements. A central transaction service joins those probabilities to purchases and manages review/audit records. Local chemical processing reduces repeated transfers and permits limited offline work; central purchase history supports the frequency feature. An edge-only design cannot reliably see cross-device activity. Cloud-only operation simplifies updates but adds connectivity and data-governance dependencies.')
    p('Use request/response scoring for a purchase with all required inputs. Use asynchronous queues for delayed laboratory results, explanations and analyst review. A pending lab result returns pending/manual review, rather than an invented chemical score. Offline reconciliation uses microbatches of up to 32 with a bounded waiting time; streaming calls use batch 1. The measured benchmark supports this design but does not exercise a deployed server.')
    h('Cache, failure and rollback')
    p('Cache chemical probabilities using sample ID, laboratory-record version and chemical-model version. Invalidate after measurement corrections or model changes. Use transaction IDs as idempotency keys to prevent duplicate review tasks. Keep failed jobs in a retry/dead-letter queue. Missing or incompatible chemistry routes to manual review; an optional transaction-only fallback must be explicitly labelled as reduced coverage. Never silently substitute chemical inputs.')
    p('Deploy a model/preprocessor/threshold bundle atomically. Retain the previous validated version and roll back on schema errors, unexplained flag-rate spikes or latency failures. During outage, queue transactions for review or apply the approved transaction-only fallback; the system must not automatically declare the purchase genuine or reject it as fraud.')
