    p('Chemistry reduces missed declaration inconsistencies but increases false alarms and requires expensive laboratory input. Lower risk thresholds generally favour recall and increase review volume; higher thresholds can miss anomalies. Thresholds must be tuned with validation outcomes and explicit costs, never adjusted to improve reported test scores. Adding a larger network is not justified by the tiny independent sample count.')
